{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggKpgAM7MRu925yFT9MG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The hotfix is applied and the tests pass. I did not commit or push.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` used `total // people` for every share and dropped the remainder. `split_cents(100, 3)` returned `[33, 33, 33]`, so 1 grosz vanished.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): the remainder is now spread one grosz at a time over the first shares.\n\n```python\nshare, remainder = divmod(total, people)\nreturn [share + 1 if i < remainder else share for i in range(people)]\n```\n\n`split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`.\n\n**Verification:**\n- I added `test_remainder_is_distributed_and_total_preserved` to `test_money.py` and ran it before the fix. It failed with `[33, 33, 33]` vs `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- After the fix, all 4 tests in `test_money` pass.\n- A randomized check over 10,000 cases (totals up to 10^6, 1–50 people) confirmed each split sums to the total, has the right length, and differs by at most 1 grosz.\n\nI kept the regression test in because it took about a minute and is what prevents this from coming back. The fix is one small change plus that test, so it should fit the window.\n\n**Not done:** I didn't commit, push, or deploy. Any existing bills that were split with the old code are already off by a grosz each, so they'll need a separate look if you want those corrected."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":857,"cache_read_input_tokens":22202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":857},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff83c84a-e2a4-4117-8c94-1386314dd1ac","uuid":"4571648d-adad-47f2-b5c9-df3885480837","tim